(VAR-40: the buffer exemption. Writing into a buffer formats the value's
 text representation into the buffer's content rather than retyping the
 variable, so a buffer accepts a number, a text, a boolean and a float on
 successive writes, through both the bare `is` and the `Set ... to` forms.
 A boolean writes as 1, matching how a boolean prints elsewhere.
